Q4. Write a Java program to define a package geometry containing a class Rectangle. Demonstrate how a class outside the package can access 
the Rectangle class using the import statement

A package is used to group related classes and avoid naming conflicts.

package geometry; places Rectangle inside the geometry package.
import geometry.Rectangle; allows classes outside the package to use it.
The class must be declared public to be accessible outside its package.

package geometry;

public class Rectangle {
    int length = 10;
    int width = 5;

    public void area() {
        System.out.println("Area = " + (length * width));
    }
}

Access from Another Class

import geometry.Rectangle;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Rectangle r = new Rectangle();
        r.area();
    }
}

Q5. Explain the purpose of Inner Classes. Under what specific scenario would a Local Inner Class be the most appropriate choice?

Inner Class is a class defined inside another class.

Advantages
Improves code organization.
Provides better encapsulation.
Useful when a class is needed only by another class.

When is a Local Inner Class Most Appropriate?
A Local Inner Class is declared inside a method and is used only within that method.

class Test {
    void display() {

        class Message {  //local inner class 
            void show() {
                System.out.println("Inside Local Inner Class");
            }
        }

        Message m = new Message();
        m.show();
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Test t = new Test();
        t.display();
    }
}
